(1760074, 239698, 43463, '<td valign="top">Love the colors here and the composition. The green picks compliment the red of the guitar very nicely - hee they exist in harmony since we are also invoking music just by looking at the objects. My only critique is the background detracts from the main focus. If the background was a solid, flat and deep black it really would have made the red guitar and the green picks litteraly "pop" off of the screen. As it is,  the texture of the black background is distracting and the "flat" greyish black tone does help the image "pop".</td>', 'Love the colors here and the composition. The green picks compliment the red of the guitar very nicely - hee they exist in harmony since we are also invoking music just by looking at the objects. My only critique is the background detracts from the main focus. If the background was a solid, flat and deep black it really would have made the red guitar and the green picks litteraly "pop" off of the screen. As it is,  the texture of the black background is distracting and the "flat" greyish black tone does help the image "pop".', '2005-10-05 03:03:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1760091, 240495, 29904, '<td valign="top">Wish this was brighter, taken at dusk?<br/>Very pretty</td>', 'Wish this was brighter, taken at dusk?Very pretty', '2005-10-05 03:10:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1760092, 240191, 43463, '<td valign="top">Very creative! Love the purples and yellows in this one. Some of those purple hues are nice, deep rich ones (those on the far right) that give this image a "tasty" appeal. The only critique is that because you had to freeze the lemons together to shape the bowl we don''t get to see the texture of those lemons or the rich inviting colors. The ice obsures our view of the veins and beautiful yellow hues of the sliced lemons. Hmmm, toothpicks would not have worked to keep the shape but mayhap perhaps a light paste around the rind to glue it to a clear glass bowl would have helped so that the inner texture and color of the lemon would have been visible?? Just a thought.</td>', 'Very creative! Love the purples and yellows in this one. Some of those purple hues are nice, deep rich ones (those on the far right) that give this image a "tasty" appeal. The only critique is that because you had to freeze the lemons together to shape the bowl we don''t get to see the texture of those lemons or the rich inviting colors. The ice obsures our view of the veins and beautiful yellow hues of the sliced lemons. Hmmm, toothpicks would not have worked to keep the shape but mayhap perhaps a light paste around the rind to glue it to a clear glass bowl would have helped so that the inner texture and color of the lemon would have been visible?? Just a thought.', '2005-10-05 03:11:50.000000', NULL, 1),
