(1769773, 239818, 43844, '<td valign="top">Brilliant shot.  You got punch in the yellow from good sunlight and yet kept the deep blue sky smooth and even.  Love it.</td>', 'Brilliant shot.  You got punch in the yellow from good sunlight and yet kept the deep blue sky smooth and even.  Love it.', '2005-10-08 11:51:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769776, 240457, 44597, '<td valign="top">Would give some of those with colour blindness hell!!!</td>', 'Would give some of those with colour blindness hell!!!', '2005-10-08 11:52:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769777, 238752, 43844, '<td valign="top">Awesome!  Great idea, great colors, great execution.  Why couldn''t I think of this myself :)</td>', 'Awesome!  Great idea, great colors, great execution.  Why couldn''t I think of this myself :)', '2005-10-08 11:52:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769781, 240129, 43844, '<td valign="top">This is my highest rated picture from those I felt didn''t quite emphasize complimentary colors.  There is green in there but the focus in clearly on the juxtaposition of the red bulb to white bulbs.  Beautiful composition.</td>', 'This is my highest rated picture from those I felt didn''t quite emphasize complimentary colors.  There is green in there but the focus in clearly on the juxtaposition of the red bulb to white bulbs.  Beautiful composition.', '2005-10-08 11:55:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769788, 240497, 43844, '<td valign="top">Wow!  Love this shot.  Not only is it a great semi-macro nature shot but you even stuck to the challenge theme.  Amazing to think these little wings can support that bubble butt of a bee.</td>', 'Wow!  Love this shot.  Not only is it a great semi-macro nature shot but you even stuck to the challenge theme.  Amazing to think these little wings can support that bubble butt of a bee.', '2005-10-08 11:57:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769791, 240480, 43844, '<td valign="top">I''m new to this forum but I''ve noticed colorful bird shots often do well.  That said, this one is truly brilliant.  Love the emotional connection with the bird''s eye.  Can we make his head green rather than blue to highlight the color complement?  Just kidding - great shot!</td>', 'I''m new to this forum but I''ve noticed colorful bird shots often do well.  That said, this one is truly brilliant.  Love the emotional connection with the bird''s eye.  Can we make his head green rather than blue to highlight the color complement?  Just kidding - great shot!', '2005-10-08 12:00:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769793, 237901, 43844, '<td valign="top">If I ever learn to do great water action shots and find myself lucky enough to capture a splash the way you did, I will be...happy.  Great shot, good job sticking with the challenge theme.</td>', 'If I ever learn to do great water action shots and find myself lucky enough to capture a splash the way you did, I will be...happy.  Great shot, good job sticking with the challenge theme.', '2005-10-08 12:01:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769798, 240586, 43844, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you already know this is an absolutely great shot.  But what I want to know is how did you keep the candle from melting?  Is it in front of the blue flame as opposed to atop it?  Regardless - brilliant work.  Print worthy.</td>', 'I''m sure you already know this is an absolutely great shot.  But what I want to know is how did you keep the candle from melting?  Is it in front of the blue flame as opposed to atop it?  Regardless - brilliant work.  Print worthy.', '2005-10-08 12:04:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769804, 238451, 43844, '<td valign="top">Love the pose, love the concept, great complement, but most of all great execution.  There are water shots and there is THIS shot.  Well done.  I hope it was Vodka with grenadine!</td>', 'Love the pose, love the concept, great complement, but most of all great execution.  There are water shots and there is THIS shot.  Well done.  I hope it was Vodka with grenadine!', '2005-10-08 12:09:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769806, 240591, 43844, '<td valign="top">Very professional, great studio set-up.  Love the thought, imagery and execution.  Well done.</td>', 'Very professional, great studio set-up.  Love the thought, imagery and execution.  Well done.', '2005-10-08 12:10:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769810, 240493, 43844, '<td valign="top">You should have had a disclosure: "no animals were hurt in the shooting of this challenge..."  Great job, great picture.</td>', 'You should have had a disclosure: "no animals were hurt in the shooting of this challenge..."  Great job, great picture.', '2005-10-08 12:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769814, 240059, 43844, '<td valign="top">I looked for praying mantis in my youth and rarely found them.  You deserve kudos just for finding one but then there is the picture...even better.  Great job.</td>', 'I looked for praying mantis in my youth and rarely found them.  You deserve kudos just for finding one but then there is the picture...even better.  Great job.', '2005-10-08 12:14:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769815, 238933, 43844, '<td valign="top">Simple idea but great execution.  Good job</td>', 'Simple idea but great execution.  Good job', '2005-10-08 12:14:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769819, 240592, 43844, '<td valign="top">I generally get tired of flower shots but this one made me stop and think "wow, where can I find one of those?"  Love the sharpness of the thin dark line on the petals</td>', 'I generally get tired of flower shots but this one made me stop and think "wow, where can I find one of those?"  Love the sharpness of the thin dark line on the petals', '2005-10-08 12:16:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769820, 240232, 43844, '<td valign="top">Love the concept.  Great model and good pose.  A few stray hairs and shin on the left but, hey! it''s better than whatever I could have done.  Great shot.</td>', 'Love the concept.  Great model and good pose.  A few stray hairs and shin on the left but, hey! it''s better than whatever I could have done.  Great shot.', '2005-10-08 12:17:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769823, 240457, 43844, '<td valign="top">Double down!  These chips look brand new!  Great idea, composition and execution.  Congrats.</td>', 'Double down!  These chips look brand new!  Great idea, composition and execution.  Congrats.', '2005-10-08 12:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769826, 239504, 43844, '<td valign="top">There are lots of color turning leaves in this challenge but this one I love.  I grew up in Canada where these colors fill the season but never took the time to look this closely at them.  Beautiful.</td>', 'There are lots of color turning leaves in this challenge but this one I love.  I grew up in Canada where these colors fill the season but never took the time to look this closely at them.  Beautiful.', '2005-10-08 12:20:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769830, 240284, 43844, '<td valign="top">Simple yet smart.  Their position actually transmits a certain emotion.  Great studio shot.</td>', 'Simple yet smart.  Their position actually transmits a certain emotion.  Great studio shot.', '2005-10-08 12:21:07.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1769835, 238742, 43844, '<td valign="top">Great idea, great shot.  Good job.</td>', 'Great idea, great shot.  Good job.', '2005-10-08 12:22:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769852, 239601, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The complementary colours I see in your image are <br/>blue/yellow.<br/> <br/>The challenge called for "two complementary colors to compose your photograph" but your photo shows more than two colours, violet, green, as well as neutrals black, white and greys... and that dilutes the visual effect of a single colour against its opposite (complementary) colour. <br/>I think your photo would have been stronger if you had grouped the yellow containers with the blue labels and cropped tightly around them. The resulting photo would have been a very interesting geometric composition.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The complementary colours I see in your image are blue/yellow. The challenge called for "two complementary colors to compose your photograph" but your photo shows more than two colours, violet, green, as well as neutrals black, white and greys... and that dilutes the visual effect of a single colour against its opposite (complementary) colour. I think your photo would have been stronger if you had grouped the yellow containers with the blue labels and cropped tightly around them. The resulting photo would have been a very interesting geometric composition.', '2005-10-08 12:33:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769855, 237469, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-08 12:35:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769856, 239904, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-08 12:35:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769857, 240073, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-08 12:36:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769858, 238183, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. <br/> <br/>Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.<br/> <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture.  Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-08 12:37:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769860, 240610, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Black and white are neutrals and not colours at all, and therefore they cannot be complementary colours... white shows the presence of light, and black shows the absence of light. Black and white areas next to each other do demonstrate high contrast, but high contrast gives a different visual effect than complementary colours do in a picture. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-08 12:38:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769868, 240247, 43329, '<td valign="top">This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  "complementary colours" are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours ("subtractive colour") or a system of Red, Green and Blue ("additive colour") as their primary colours. <br/>For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable.<br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of "opposite" colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for "two complementary colors to compose your photograph" but your photo shows reds, blues, yellows and greens, and it gives the vibrant effect of primary colours, rather than the effect of a single colour against its opposite (complementary) colour. <br/> <br/>I think your photo is a great demonstration of primary colour and texture, but not of complementary colours. Sorry!<br/> <br/></td>', 'This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  "complementary colours" are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours ("subtractive colour") or a system of Red, Green and Blue ("additive colour") as their primary colours. For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable. Complementary colours are pairs of "opposite" colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for "two complementary colors to compose your photograph" but your photo shows reds, blues, yellows and greens, and it gives the vibrant effect of primary colours, rather than the effect of a single colour against its opposite (complementary) colour.  I think your photo is a great demonstration of primary colour and texture, but not of complementary colours. Sorry! ', '2005-10-08 12:44:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769878, 238147, 43329, '<td valign="top">This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  "complementary colours" are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours ("subtractive colour") or a system of Red, Green and Blue ("additive colour") as their primary colours. <br/>For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable.<br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of "opposite" colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for "two complementary colors to compose your photograph" but your photo shows yellow and orange as well as red and green, and that dilutes the effect of a single colour (green) against its opposite or complementary colour (red). <br/> <br/>Nevertheless, this is a fantastic shot of the peppers and I think it''s mouthwatering good, to boot!  <br/> <br/>I think your photo would have been a stronger demonstration of complementary colours if you had replaced the yellow pepper with another red or green one and shot against a neutral background of black, white or grey. <br/></td>', 'This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  "complementary colours" are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours ("subtractive colour") or a system of Red, Green and Blue ("additive colour") as their primary colours. For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable. Complementary colours are pairs of "opposite" colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for "two complementary colors to compose your photograph" but your photo shows yellow and orange as well as red and green, and that dilutes the effect of a single colour (green) against its opposite or complementary colour (red).  Nevertheless, this is a fantastic shot of the peppers and I think it''s mouthwatering good, to boot!   I think your photo would have been a stronger demonstration of complementary colours if you had replaced the yellow pepper with another red or green one and shot against a neutral background of black, white or grey. ', '2005-10-08 12:52:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1769899, 239165, 43329, '<td valign="top">This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  complementary colours are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours (subtractive colour) or a system of Red, Green and Blue (additive colour) as their primary colours. <br/>For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable.<br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of opposite colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for two complementary colors to compose your photograph but in your photo I see red and blue as well as violet and yellow, and that dilutes the effect of tones of a single colour (violet) against tones of its opposite or complementary colour (yellow). <br/> <br/>I think your photo would have been a stronger demonstration of complementary colours if you had replaced the central flowers with another bouquet of flowers closer in tones to violet. <br/> <br/>Nevertheless, this is a great shot of the textures in the wreath.   <br/></td>', 'This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  complementary colours are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours (subtractive colour) or a system of Red, Green and Blue (additive colour) as their primary colours. For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable. Complementary colours are pairs of opposite colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for two complementary colors to compose your photograph but in your photo I see red and blue as well as violet and yellow, and that dilutes the effect of tones of a single colour (violet) against tones of its opposite or complementary colour (yellow).  I think your photo would have been a stronger demonstration of complementary colours if you had replaced the central flowers with another bouquet of flowers closer in tones to violet.  Nevertheless, this is a great shot of the textures in the wreath.   ', '2005-10-08 13:01:07.000000', NULL, 1),
