(1770529, 237788, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of opposite colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for two complementary colors to compose your photograph but in your photo I see purplish brown, dull yellow and bright green, as well as the reddish orange of the basketball. The addition of the extra colours dilutes the visual effect of tones of a single predominating colour against tones of its opposite or complementary colour. <br/> <br/>I think your submission would have been a stronger demonstration of complementary colours if you had chosen a background that of a complementary colour to the red-oranges of the basketball, for instance, by photographing it against a blue basketball jersey, or a blue-green toned towel, to keep the sports metaphor.<br/> <br/>Great closeup shot of the textures of the ball and the ground!    <br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of opposite colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The challenge called for two complementary colors to compose your photograph but in your photo I see purplish brown, dull yellow and bright green, as well as the reddish orange of the basketball. The addition of the extra colours dilutes the visual effect of tones of a single predominating colour against tones of its opposite or complementary colour.  I think your submission would have been a stronger demonstration of complementary colours if you had chosen a background that of a complementary colour to the red-oranges of the basketball, for instance, by photographing it against a blue basketball jersey, or a blue-green toned towel, to keep the sports metaphor. Great closeup shot of the textures of the ball and the ground!    ', '2005-10-08 19:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770533, 240242, 43774, '<td valign="top">I don''t think the purple is prominent enough to be part of the 2 complementary colours. It looks mostly black except in the bottom left corner.</td>', 'I don''t think the purple is prominent enough to be part of the 2 complementary colours. It looks mostly black except in the bottom left corner.', '2005-10-08 19:06:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770535, 239746, 43774, '<td valign="top">Focus looks off and the glare from the lights is too harsh.</td>', 'Focus looks off and the glare from the lights is too harsh.', '2005-10-08 19:06:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770537, 240489, 43774, '<td valign="top">Too many colours, I don''t see 2 complementary colours.</td>', 'Too many colours, I don''t see 2 complementary colours.', '2005-10-08 19:07:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770538, 240129, 43774, '<td valign="top">Not really complementary colours.</td>', 'Not really complementary colours.', '2005-10-08 19:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770539, 239733, 43774, '<td valign="top">Doesn''t really fit the theme of 2 complementary colours.</td>', 'Doesn''t really fit the theme of 2 complementary colours.', '2005-10-08 19:08:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770540, 238556, 43774, '<td valign="top">Fits the theme but the colours are too bright and over saturated. Focus seems off too.</td>', 'Fits the theme but the colours are too bright and over saturated. Focus seems off too.', '2005-10-08 19:08:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770541, 239608, 43774, '<td valign="top">Odd photo, nothing really appealing about it, focus seems off.</td>', 'Odd photo, nothing really appealing about it, focus seems off.', '2005-10-08 19:09:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770549, 238435, 43329, '<td valign="top">This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  complementary colours are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a colour wheel based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours (subtractive colour) or a colour wheel of Red, Green and Blue (additive colour) as their primary colours. <br/>For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable.<br/> <br/>Your image appears to be composed not so much in complementary colours as in a monochromatic scheme, in that it is mostly pinks, or pale tones of red-orange. The complementary colour to this would be a greenish-blue...and in fact t his colour does exist in your photo. (Try inverting the colours in Photoshop to test this out.) However, my eye reads this cyan colour as being white highlights along the top of the head and the feathers. <br/> <br/>Nevertheless, this is a great photo of a beautiful bird, and the colours are phenomenal! A small adjustment in the colours in the background would have made a huge difference in showing complementary colours.<br/></td>', 'This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  complementary colours are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a colour wheel based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours (subtractive colour) or a colour wheel of Red, Green and Blue (additive colour) as their primary colours. For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable. Your image appears to be composed not so much in complementary colours as in a monochromatic scheme, in that it is mostly pinks, or pale tones of red-orange. The complementary colour to this would be a greenish-blue...and in fact t his colour does exist in your photo. (Try inverting the colours in Photoshop to test this out.) However, my eye reads this cyan colour as being white highlights along the top of the head and the feathers.  Nevertheless, this is a great photo of a beautiful bird, and the colours are phenomenal! A small adjustment in the colours in the background would have made a huge difference in showing complementary colours.', '2005-10-08 19:17:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770560, 240410, 43329, '<td valign="top">This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  complementary colours are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours (subtractive colour) or a system of Red, Green and Blue (additive colour) as their primary colours. <br/>For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable.<br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The main colours in your image are the red of the dice and the blue in the background. The white spots are neutral, and the bubbles carry a greenish reflection, but the dominant colours are red and blue. <br/>I think your photo would have been a stronger submission if you had used a rich dark green in the background to enhance the effect of the dice, or else kept the beautiful blue background and made the dice closer to a yellow-orange so as to enhance the complementary contrast with the background.<br/></td>', 'This was a difficult challenge to work on... people''s opinions differ on what the  complementary colours are, mainly depending on whether they are working with a system based on Red, Yellow and Blue as their primary colours (subtractive colour) or a system of Red, Green and Blue (additive colour) as their primary colours. For this challenge, I believe either system is acceptable. Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The main colours in your image are the red of the dice and the blue in the background. The white spots are neutral, and the bubbles carry a greenish reflection, but the dominant colours are red and blue. I think your photo would have been a stronger submission if you had used a rich dark green in the background to enhance the effect of the dice, or else kept the beautiful blue background and made the dice closer to a yellow-orange so as to enhance the complementary contrast with the background.', '2005-10-08 19:23:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770570, 240173, 45194, '<td valign="top">Outstanding photo! The best I''ve seen having been through every picture now.  Nearly a 10, most DEFINATELY a 9!</td>', 'Outstanding photo! The best I''ve seen having been through every picture now.  Nearly a 10, most DEFINATELY a 9!', '2005-10-08 19:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770571, 240538, 43329, '<td valign="top">The complementary colours I see in your image are yellow/violet, but the addition of the strong green from the leaves of the plant change the effect of the complementary colours. <br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The main colours in your image are yellow and violet.<br/>I think your photo would have been stronger if you could somehow have de-emphasized the green or else shot the photo with just the blossoms and not the leaves.</td>', 'The complementary colours I see in your image are yellow/violet, but the addition of the strong green from the leaves of the plant change the effect of the complementary colours.  Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The main colours in your image are yellow and violet.I think your photo would have been stronger if you could somehow have de-emphasized the green or else shot the photo with just the blossoms and not the leaves.', '2005-10-08 19:27:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770573, 240173, 42005, '<td valign="top">This is just delightful to view.  Amazing use of yellow......have never seen that and like it.</td>', 'This is just delightful to view.  Amazing use of yellow......have never seen that and like it.', '2005-10-08 19:29:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770578, 240556, 43329, '<td valign="top">What an elegant composition! <br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Unfortunately, the yellow colour you show in the upper leaves is not the complementary colour to the green of the lower leaves... you would need to have a redder tone in the upper leaves, and a corresponding shift towards a blue-green in the lower leaves to achieve the complementary pair of red/green.  <br/> <br/>Regardless, this is a beautiful image, and despite the fact that it didn''t meet the requirements of the challenge, I think it is lovely.</td>', 'What an elegant composition!  Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Unfortunately, the yellow colour you show in the upper leaves is not the complementary colour to the green of the lower leaves... you would need to have a redder tone in the upper leaves, and a corresponding shift towards a blue-green in the lower leaves to achieve the complementary pair of red/green.   Regardless, this is a beautiful image, and despite the fact that it didn''t meet the requirements of the challenge, I think it is lovely.', '2005-10-08 19:33:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770583, 240444, 43329, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful composition! <br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Unfortunately, the yellow colour you show in the center of the flower is not the complementary colour to the red of the petals... you would need to have a more green tone in the center of the flower to achieve the complementary pair of red/green, or a more blue-violet hue in the petals to achieve the complementary pair of yellow/violet.  <br/> <br/>Regardless, this is a strong composition, despite the fact that it didn''t meet the requirements of the challenge.</td>', 'What a beautiful composition!  Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Unfortunately, the yellow colour you show in the center of the flower is not the complementary colour to the red of the petals... you would need to have a more green tone in the center of the flower to achieve the complementary pair of red/green, or a more blue-violet hue in the petals to achieve the complementary pair of yellow/violet.   Regardless, this is a strong composition, despite the fact that it didn''t meet the requirements of the challenge.', '2005-10-08 19:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770595, 240074, 43329, '<td valign="top">What a strong design! <br/> <br/>Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Unfortunately, the yellow colour you show in the triangles on the sides is not the complementary colour to the red in the center... you would need to have a more green tone on the sides to achieve the complementary pair of red/green, or a more blue-violet hue in the center to achieve the complementary pair of yellow/violet.  <br/> <br/>Regardless, this is a very striking design, despite the fact that it didn''t meet the requirements of the challenge.</td>', 'What a strong design!  Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Unfortunately, the yellow colour you show in the triangles on the sides is not the complementary colour to the red in the center... you would need to have a more green tone on the sides to achieve the complementary pair of red/green, or a more blue-violet hue in the center to achieve the complementary pair of yellow/violet.   Regardless, this is a very striking design, despite the fact that it didn''t meet the requirements of the challenge.', '2005-10-08 19:42:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1770624, 240591, 19936, '<td valign="top">My favorite of the challenge.  Well done!</td>', 'My favorite of the challenge.  Well done!', '2005-10-08 20:06:24.000000', NULL, 1),
