(1773697, 238071, 43329, '<td valign="top">You need to have added a range of blue tones ranging from indigo to cyan in order to demonstrate complementary colour contrast in this photo. Nice textures in the surface, though!</td>', 'You need to have added a range of blue tones ranging from indigo to cyan in order to demonstrate complementary colour contrast in this photo. Nice textures in the surface, though!', '2005-10-10 09:17:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773698, 240440, 43329, '<td valign="top">Your car should have been more yellow than red to demonstrate complementary colour contrast against the colours in the background.</td>', 'Your car should have been more yellow than red to demonstrate complementary colour contrast against the colours in the background.', '2005-10-10 09:18:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773700, 239745, 43329, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot of the crane, but you could have shot at a different angle and/or cropped a bit tighter to emphasize the orange-yellow complementary colour contrast on the equipment.</td>', 'Very nice shot of the crane, but you could have shot at a different angle and/or cropped a bit tighter to emphasize the orange-yellow complementary colour contrast on the equipment.', '2005-10-10 09:20:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773703, 240198, 43329, '<td valign="top">Yellow and green are not complementary colours... your model should have worn a red coloured shirt to provide complementary colour contrast in this nice portrait.</td>', 'Yellow and green are not complementary colours... your model should have worn a red coloured shirt to provide complementary colour contrast in this nice portrait.', '2005-10-10 09:21:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773704, 240607, 43329, '<td valign="top">Fine abstract arrangement of leaves, but you needed to show more red and not yellow to demonstrate complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'Fine abstract arrangement of leaves, but you needed to show more red and not yellow to demonstrate complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:22:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773709, 240229, 43329, '<td valign="top">Great shot of the temple, but your main complementary colours of the red bricks and the green foliage are diluted with the yellow/violet colours on the roofline and the blue/orange in the windows. You could have cropped tighter to the building to show just red and green to demonstrate the complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'Great shot of the temple, but your main complementary colours of the red bricks and the green foliage are diluted with the yellow/violet colours on the roofline and the blue/orange in the windows. You could have cropped tighter to the building to show just red and green to demonstrate the complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:25:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773711, 240454, 43329, '<td valign="top">The complementary colour for red is green and for yellow is blue-violet. Your photo does not demonstrate complementary colour contrast. Nevertheless it is an interesting abstract arrangement of bright colours and interesting textures.</td>', 'The complementary colour for red is green and for yellow is blue-violet. Your photo does not demonstrate complementary colour contrast. Nevertheless it is an interesting abstract arrangement of bright colours and interesting textures.', '2005-10-10 09:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773713, 239841, 38921, '<td valign="top">Looks like the reds got blown out as there is no detail on the upper left third of the balls.</td>', 'Looks like the reds got blown out as there is no detail on the upper left third of the balls.', '2005-10-10 09:29:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773714, 238048, 43329, '<td valign="top">Yellow and green are not complementary colours... your scene should have included a dark blue-violet door to provide complementary colour contrast against the yellow wall, or else a red coloured wall to give complementary contrast to the green door.</td>', 'Yellow and green are not complementary colours... your scene should have included a dark blue-violet door to provide complementary colour contrast against the yellow wall, or else a red coloured wall to give complementary contrast to the green door.', '2005-10-10 09:30:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773715, 240412, 43329, '<td valign="top">Fine splash shot, but to show a the complementary colour for the strawberry, your background would have been a pale green tone. Or else, keep the blue toned background and splash something yellow/orange into the glass!</td>', 'Fine splash shot, but to show a the complementary colour for the strawberry, your background would have been a pale green tone. Or else, keep the blue toned background and splash something yellow/orange into the glass!', '2005-10-10 09:31:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773716, 238777, 43329, '<td valign="top">Wonderful wide shot of the peppers, but there are too many reds, oranges and yellows here to  allow you to demonstrate complementary pairs of colours. Perhaps a closer shot of just the red and green peppers would have been more successful?</td>', 'Wonderful wide shot of the peppers, but there are too many reds, oranges and yellows here to  allow you to demonstrate complementary pairs of colours. Perhaps a closer shot of just the red and green peppers would have been more successful?', '2005-10-10 09:34:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773717, 240495, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>The colours in this photo are so desaturated that the effect of complementary colours is lost. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.<br/> <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The colours in this photo are so desaturated that the effect of complementary colours is lost. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:35:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773720, 240543, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/> <br/>The red of the flag is lost against all the blue toned background. Your shot would have been a more successful demonstration of complementary contrast if you had cropped tight around the red and shown some of the green foliage around it as contrast.</td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other.  The red of the flag is lost against all the blue toned background. Your shot would have been a more successful demonstration of complementary contrast if you had cropped tight around the red and shown some of the green foliage around it as contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:37:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773722, 240081, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/> <br/>The red of the barns is lost against all the green, brown and blue toned background. Your shot would have been a more successful demonstration of complementary contrast if you had shot from a different angle so the barns aren''t so far apart, and cropped tighter around the red and shown some of the green foliage around it as contrast.</td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other.  The red of the barns is lost against all the green, brown and blue toned background. Your shot would have been a more successful demonstration of complementary contrast if you had shot from a different angle so the barns aren''t so far apart, and cropped tighter around the red and shown some of the green foliage around it as contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:39:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773724, 240606, 43329, '<td valign="top">This would have been a more successful demonstration of the effect of complementary colours if you had removed the vase with the yellow flowers and just gone with the red/green complementary contrast.</td>', 'This would have been a more successful demonstration of the effect of complementary colours if you had removed the vase with the yellow flowers and just gone with the red/green complementary contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:40:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773729, 238206, 43329, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately, this fine photo does not show complementary contrast. Your flowers should have been a violet-tinged red to show up the yellow-green in the foliage. Nice shot and great cropping around the flowers!</td>', 'Unfortunately, this fine photo does not show complementary contrast. Your flowers should have been a violet-tinged red to show up the yellow-green in the foliage. Nice shot and great cropping around the flowers!', '2005-10-10 09:42:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773730, 239567, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>The colours in this photo are so desaturated that the effect of complementary colours is lost. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.<br/> <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The colours in this photo are so desaturated that the effect of complementary colours is lost. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:43:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773735, 240186, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>The red-tipped yellow petals would require a blue-violet background to demonstrate complementary colours. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.<br/> <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The red-tipped yellow petals would require a blue-violet background to demonstrate complementary colours. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:46:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773737, 240065, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>The green foliage would require a red-toned flower to demonstrate complementary colours. <br/> <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The green foliage would require a red-toned flower to demonstrate complementary colours.  Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:49:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773738, 238923, 43329, '<td valign="top">The predominant colour in this photo is the blue in the lower half. The child''s jacket needs to be more orange-yellow to provide a complementary colour contrast. In addition, the green grass and the colours of the park scene above the child''s head take away from the contrast of two colours against each other.<br/></td>', 'The predominant colour in this photo is the blue in the lower half. The child''s jacket needs to be more orange-yellow to provide a complementary colour contrast. In addition, the green grass and the colours of the park scene above the child''s head take away from the contrast of two colours against each other.', '2005-10-10 09:51:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773741, 237512, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>Apart from the flashes of red in the children''s clothing, all the colours are so desaturated that the blues and the oranges do not demonstrate the effect of complementary colour contrast. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.<br/> <br/>It''s a touching photo, though, and sent me looking for more information on Sapa.</td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. Apart from the flashes of red in the children''s clothing, all the colours are so desaturated that the blues and the oranges do not demonstrate the effect of complementary colour contrast. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours. It''s a touching photo, though, and sent me looking for more information on Sapa.', '2005-10-10 09:53:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773747, 240489, 43329, '<td valign="top">The predominant colours in this photo are green tones. To demonstrate complementary contrast, you would have needed more red-orange colours in the flowers. However, if you had changed your angle and shot the goldfish with the bronze of the statue or the green waterlily leaves, you would have had a fine demonstration of complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'The predominant colours in this photo are green tones. To demonstrate complementary contrast, you would have needed more red-orange colours in the flowers. However, if you had changed your angle and shot the goldfish with the bronze of the statue or the green waterlily leaves, you would have had a fine demonstration of complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 09:56:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773756, 239608, 43329, '<td valign="top">The red and the dull green can be considered complementary colours, but the yellow light destroys the effect. Great composition, nice visual balance, but the LED needs to be green to demonstrate complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'The red and the dull green can be considered complementary colours, but the yellow light destroys the effect. Great composition, nice visual balance, but the LED needs to be green to demonstrate complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:00:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773762, 237677, 43329, '<td valign="top">In order to show complementary colour contrast, the center of this flower should have been a blue-green similar to the colour of the stem. Nice closeup shot and good composition arrangement. I like the contrast of the spiky pink petals against the black background, but it''s not complementary contrast.</td>', 'In order to show complementary colour contrast, the center of this flower should have been a blue-green similar to the colour of the stem. Nice closeup shot and good composition arrangement. I like the contrast of the spiky pink petals against the black background, but it''s not complementary contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:03:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773767, 239733, 43329, '<td valign="top">Great closeup of the beautifully patterned butterfly against the yellow flower. Unfortunate that the complementary colour to the green leaves would have been a violet-tinged red. If the leaves were more of a blue to blue-violet tone, this fine photo would also have demonstrated the complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'Great closeup of the beautifully patterned butterfly against the yellow flower. Unfortunate that the complementary colour to the green leaves would have been a violet-tinged red. If the leaves were more of a blue to blue-violet tone, this fine photo would also have demonstrated the complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:07:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773771, 240386, 43329, '<td valign="top">Too many complementary pairs... take out the blue and the orange and your arrangement of child''s toys does demonstrate complementary colour contrast.<br/>Nice shot of the toys though!<br/></td>', 'Too many complementary pairs... take out the blue and the orange and your arrangement of child''s toys does demonstrate complementary colour contrast.Nice shot of the toys though!', '2005-10-10 10:08:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773778, 239163, 43329, '<td valign="top">Your photo would have demonstrated the effects of complementary colour contrast if you had changed your angle to show the violet flower in the middle against the goldenrod, and then cropped tightly to show just the violet and the yellow colours.</td>', 'Your photo would have demonstrated the effects of complementary colour contrast if you had changed your angle to show the violet flower in the middle against the goldenrod, and then cropped tightly to show just the violet and the yellow colours.', '2005-10-10 10:11:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773782, 240045, 43329, '<td valign="top">The background of this photo needs to show more violet tones to provide complementary colour contrast against the yellows. Nice car!</td>', 'The background of this photo needs to show more violet tones to provide complementary colour contrast against the yellows. Nice car!', '2005-10-10 10:13:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773789, 239676, 43329, '<td valign="top">Too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If you could have shot the blue butterfly against the yellow flower and then cropped tightly to eliminate any red or green, or else if you had shot just the red and green flowers, you would have had a better demonstration of complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'Too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If you could have shot the blue butterfly against the yellow flower and then cropped tightly to eliminate any red or green, or else if you had shot just the red and green flowers, you would have had a better demonstration of complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:15:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773798, 240480, 43329, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot of the bird''s plumage!<br/> <br/>Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the bird''s eye and beak could have shown more orange against the blue feathers on its head, that would have been a great demonstration of complementary colour contrast.<br/> <br/>Nevertheless, this is a great photo of a colourful bird.</td>', 'Fantastic shot of the bird''s plumage! Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the bird''s eye and beak could have shown more orange against the blue feathers on its head, that would have been a great demonstration of complementary colour contrast. Nevertheless, this is a great photo of a colourful bird.', '2005-10-10 10:17:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773805, 239744, 43329, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the foliage behind the bright red bird had been the bright green that it is at the bottom, that would have been a great demonstration of complementary colour contrast.<br/> <br/>Nevertheless, this is a nice photo of a colourful bird.</td>', 'Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the foliage behind the bright red bird had been the bright green that it is at the bottom, that would have been a great demonstration of complementary colour contrast. Nevertheless, this is a nice photo of a colourful bird.', '2005-10-10 10:19:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773813, 240270, 43329, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If you had selected, say the blue bottle with the spirals and either the yellow bottle or the orange bottle, you would have had a good demonstration of complementary colour contrast. Nice blue tones in the background and in the rocks would have added to the effect.<br/></td>', 'Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If you had selected, say the blue bottle with the spirals and either the yellow bottle or the orange bottle, you would have had a good demonstration of complementary colour contrast. Nice blue tones in the background and in the rocks would have added to the effect.', '2005-10-10 10:22:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773818, 240047, 43329, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the shot had shown more of the bird''s orange eye and beak against the blue feathers of its head, and the photo been cropped to remove the green, yellow and red tones in the body, that would have been a better demonstration of complementary colour contrast.<br/> <br/>Nevertheless, I love the colourful look in the bird''s eye!</td>', 'Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the shot had shown more of the bird''s orange eye and beak against the blue feathers of its head, and the photo been cropped to remove the green, yellow and red tones in the body, that would have been a better demonstration of complementary colour contrast. Nevertheless, I love the colourful look in the bird''s eye!', '2005-10-10 10:26:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773822, 238785, 43329, '<td valign="top">Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the photo was cropped to remove the blue feathers on the bird''s body, that would have been a great demonstration of complementary colour contrast between red and green.<br/> <br/>Nevertheless, this is a great photo of a colourful bird.</td>', 'Unfortunately there are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If the photo was cropped to remove the blue feathers on the bird''s body, that would have been a great demonstration of complementary colour contrast between red and green. Nevertheless, this is a great photo of a colourful bird.', '2005-10-10 10:28:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773824, 240181, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>The colours are so desaturated that the blues and the oranges do not demonstrate the effect of complementary colour contrast. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The colours are so desaturated that the blues and the oranges do not demonstrate the effect of complementary colour contrast. Your image demonstrates a duotone effect rather than the effect of complementary colours.', '2005-10-10 10:29:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773828, 240576, 43329, '<td valign="top">Actually, the yellow tone in the lower right takes away from the red/green complementary colour contrast in this photo.</td>', 'Actually, the yellow tone in the lower right takes away from the red/green complementary colour contrast in this photo.', '2005-10-10 10:30:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773837, 239191, 43329, '<td valign="top">There are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If your shot showed only the blue and yellow toys, with the same composition and depth of field, you would have had a fine demonstration of complementary colour contrast. <br/>But just looking at the birds with their wierd expressions, I like them better with all their colours... more energy and more fun for carnival toys!</td>', 'There are too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. If your shot showed only the blue and yellow toys, with the same composition and depth of field, you would have had a fine demonstration of complementary colour contrast. But just looking at the birds with their wierd expressions, I like them better with all their colours... more energy and more fun for carnival toys!', '2005-10-10 10:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773841, 240281, 43329, '<td valign="top">Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. <br/>The blue-green of this car calls out for more red rather than yellow in the picture, or else the orange-yellow in the trees requires more blue tones in order to demonstrate the complementary colour contrast. <br/>Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.<br/></td>', 'Complementary colours are pairs of colours that contrast strongly when compared to each other. The blue-green of this car calls out for more red rather than yellow in the picture, or else the orange-yellow in the trees requires more blue tones in order to demonstrate the complementary colour contrast. Check some of the forum discussions on complementary colours for suggestions on using colour for contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:39:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773842, 239381, 43329, '<td valign="top">Fine closeup shot of the thistle, great depth of field. Unfortunately, the green in the shot destroys the complementary colour contrast between the violet and the yellow colours.</td>', 'Fine closeup shot of the thistle, great depth of field. Unfortunately, the green in the shot destroys the complementary colour contrast between the violet and the yellow colours.', '2005-10-10 10:40:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773848, 237991, 43329, '<td valign="top">Too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite.</td>', 'Too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite.', '2005-10-10 10:41:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773853, 237907, 43329, '<td valign="top">If the greens in the foliage weren''t so bright, and if the yellow flowers in the foreground were cropped out, this would be a better demonstration of the effect of complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'If the greens in the foliage weren''t so bright, and if the yellow flowers in the foreground were cropped out, this would be a better demonstration of the effect of complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:44:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773859, 239365, 43329, '<td valign="top">Wow, nice closeup shot! Too bad that the green in the background destroys the complementary colour contrast of the yellow and the violet tones. <br/>If you had shot from a different angle to get just the flowers and then cropped to show only the yellow and the purple, this would have been a great demonstration of the effect of complementary colour contrast.</td>', 'Wow, nice closeup shot! Too bad that the green in the background destroys the complementary colour contrast of the yellow and the violet tones. If you had shot from a different angle to get just the flowers and then cropped to show only the yellow and the purple, this would have been a great demonstration of the effect of complementary colour contrast.', '2005-10-10 10:47:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773863, 239482, 43329, '<td valign="top">Too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. This is a great demonstration of a primary colour scheme with red and blue and yellow.</td>', 'Too many complementary pairs here to demonstrate the effect of one colour contrasted against its opposite. This is a great demonstration of a primary colour scheme with red and blue and yellow.', '2005-10-10 10:49:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773885, 240610, 44289, '<td valign="top">I really like the photo but it just doesn''t seem to fit the challenge.</td>', 'I really like the photo but it just doesn''t seem to fit the challenge.', '2005-10-10 11:10:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773892, 239230, 25728, '<td valign="top">The composition of this really appeals to me.</td>', 'The composition of this really appeals to me.', '2005-10-10 11:17:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773896, 239392, 25728, '<td valign="top">Nice composotion, nice framing, lovely colors...</td>', 'Nice composotion, nice framing, lovely colors...', '2005-10-10 11:23:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773897, 240354, 25728, '<td valign="top">A different shot, I like this!</td>', 'A different shot, I like this!', '2005-10-10 11:24:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1773938, 238971, 25728, '<td valign="top">I cant put my finger on exactly why, but this picture is really really appealing to me. I could also be really hungry, but it the colors I think - very vibrant.....</td>', 'I cant put my finger on exactly why, but this picture is really really appealing to me. I could also be really hungry, but it the colors I think - very vibrant.....', '2005-10-10 11:52:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774016, 239046, 36619, '<td valign="top">they almost look like two robots standing there. nice composition.</td>', 'they almost look like two robots standing there. nice composition.', '2005-10-10 12:37:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774024, 239392, 36619, '<td valign="top">really nice photo!</td>', 'really nice photo!', '2005-10-10 12:45:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774114, 238360, 42602, '<td valign="top">now THAT is one cool picture! Keep up the awesome work. Personally, I would have cropped it a little closer on the bottom, but it doesn''t look bad at all the way it is.</td>', 'now THAT is one cool picture! Keep up the awesome work. Personally, I would have cropped it a little closer on the bottom, but it doesn''t look bad at all the way it is.', '2005-10-10 13:17:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774185, 240304, 35322, '<td valign="top">cute! but not complementary!</td>', 'cute! but not complementary!', '2005-10-10 13:59:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774222, 239504, 29474, '<td valign="top">Seen this before, metatate. Not sure that I am happy with that!! It might prejudice my voting.<br/> <br/>And no ... not a "crabby control freak" ... just very serious about voting remaining anonymous. It is what makes this site work so well. A lot of the features of the site are directly in support of this, including the "baghead" one. And yes, by all means, show your friends, as long as they are not voting members of DPC.</td>', 'Seen this before, metatate. Not sure that I am happy with that!! It might prejudice my voting. And no ... not a "crabby control freak" ... just very serious about voting remaining anonymous. It is what makes this site work so well. A lot of the features of the site are directly in support of this, including the "baghead" one. And yes, by all means, show your friends, as long as they are not voting members of DPC.', '2005-10-10 14:14:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774318, 240412, 44107, '<td valign="top">I really like this photo.  The focus is great, colors are good!</td>', 'I really like this photo.  The focus is great, colors are good!', '2005-10-10 14:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774321, 238792, 44107, '<td valign="top">Nice colors, but the picture itself lacks feeling.</td>', 'Nice colors, but the picture itself lacks feeling.', '2005-10-10 14:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1774327, 240191, 44107, '<td valign="top">I''m giving this a 10. even thought the bowl looks gross.  Everything else is perfect.  Nice colors, focus and composition.</td>', 'I''m giving this a 10. even thought the bowl looks gross.  Everything else is perfect.  Nice colors, focus and composition.', '2005-10-10 14:58:58.000000', NULL, 1);
