(1779048, 237907, 36616, '<td valign="top">Great ape, great pic. Good focus, composition etc.<br/>Complementary - technically further away from true complements than many; artistically closer than many appear to have given you credit for.<br/>Unfortunately in my opinion a relatively large number of voters took an absolute idea of complements and had no flexibility with regard to shade of colour which affects the complement equally. <br/>Your shot definitely deserved to be higher placed.</td>', 'Great ape, great pic. Good focus, composition etc.Complementary - technically further away from true complements than many; artistically closer than many appear to have given you credit for.Unfortunately in my opinion a relatively large number of voters took an absolute idea of complements and had no flexibility with regard to shade of colour which affects the complement equally. Your shot definitely deserved to be higher placed.', '2005-10-12 09:40:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1779051, 239392, 32754, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for all the positive comments and critiques...I guess this image appealed to others as well as myself...this is quite a thrill to be in top 10...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-13 11:30:45.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everyone for all the positive comments and critiques...I guess this image appealed to others as well as myself...this is quite a thrill to be in top 10...', '2005-10-12 09:42:28.000000', '2005-10-13 12:30:45.000000', 0),
(1779054, 240466, 12253, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure I agree that this is "too blurry".  As is, I think it has the right ingredients for an abstract.  I''d have to see how it came out sharp to see if that was better!   <br/> <br/>You could play a bit with this shot to possibly make it stronger.  Since color is the primary focus of this abstract, perhaps you can try adjusting the white balance or levels so that the crystal does not appear toned (it has a yellow-tan tone on my monitor), and let the shape of crystal alone serve to texture the greens and reds in the background (along with some perhaps stronger greens which can also be adjusted in PS).  <br/> <br/>This was a good idea!</td>', 'I''m not sure I agree that this is "too blurry".  As is, I think it has the right ingredients for an abstract.  I''d have to see how it came out sharp to see if that was better!    You could play a bit with this shot to possibly make it stronger.  Since color is the primary focus of this abstract, perhaps you can try adjusting the white balance or levels so that the crystal does not appear toned (it has a yellow-tan tone on my monitor), and let the shape of crystal alone serve to texture the greens and reds in the background (along with some perhaps stronger greens which can also be adjusted in PS).   This was a good idea!', '2005-10-12 09:42:41.000000', NULL, 0),
